# A11y: Focus, Motion, Touch

## Focus Visible

Use `focus-visible` for keyboard-only outlines.

```css
@utility focus-ring {
  &:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-brand-500);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
}
```

## Reduced Motion

Respect user preference.

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}
```

Use utility:
```html
<div class="transition-transform motion-reduce:transition-none">
```

## Touch Targets

Minimum 44x44px for interactive elements.

```css
@utility touch-target {
  min-width: 44px;
  min-height: 44px;
}
```

## Forced Colors

Support high contrast mode.

```css
@media (forced-colors: active) {
  .btn {
    border: 1px solid CanvasText;
    forced-color-adjust: none;
  }
}
```

## Best Practices

- Never remove focus indicators
- Use semantic HTML + Tailwind
- Ensure color contrast AA minimum
- Provide text alternatives for icons
- Test with screen readers
- Avoid motion for decorative elements only
- Keep interactive areas large on touch devices
